    <fr:title text="Group Element Order">Group Element Order</fr:title>
    <fr:taxon>Definition</fr:taxon>
  </fr:frontmatter>
  <fr:mainmatter>
    <html:p>
For a group <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[G]]></fr:tex> an <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[x\in  G]]></fr:tex> define the <html:strong>order</html:strong> of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[x]]></fr:tex> be the smallest positive integer <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n]]></fr:tex> (denotes <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[|x|]]></fr:tex>) st <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[x^n=1]]></fr:tex>. If such <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n]]></fr:tex> does not exist then <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[x]]></fr:tex> is said to be of infinite order.
</html:p>
